# Pixel handoff

- Pixel is Nathan's Grok Bot art/visual agent. It can't talk to Cursor directly. It signals through GitHub PRs labeled `ready-to-test`.

## Every Nathan message
1. At the start, quietly run:
   `gh pr list --repo Nathan-Elequin/swipe --label ready-to-test --json number,title,headRefName,body`
2. Do what Nathan asked first.
3. Then, for each listed PR he hasn't already responded to in this chat, end the reply with a "Ready to test from Pixel" section (format below).

## Note format (same house style as `playtest-inbox.mdc`)
- Its own section, after everything else in the reply (after **Closed issues** if those appear): `### 🎨 Ready to test from Pixel`.
- One block per PR, started by a bold title line with the PR link.
- Bold labels, each followed by an em dash and a short line: **What it is**, **Why**, **Try this in-game** (1–3 numbered items), **To try it**.
- Write it assuming Nathan doesn't remember the context. Friend-voice, plain words.
- **To try it** is a one-line call to action: "Say **load it**." If boss-rush is already on that branch: "It's already loaded, just press F5."

Example:

```
### 🎨 Ready to test from Pixel

**[#87 Fusion Adventure + today's cards](https://github.com/Nathan-Elequin/swipe/pull/87)**
- **What it is** — Your fusion Adventure mode from yesterday plus today's Pocketwatch, Shuriken and move-arc work, all on one branch.
- **Why** — Step 1 of the cleanup: one clean branch instead of scattered local changes.
- **Try this in-game**
  1. Start Adventure: 6 random monsters, pick 2 cards six times.
  2. Use your 3 moves (winged-foot pips, curved arrows beside Take), then undo one.
  3. Longbow should hit for 5 with an even number of monsters.
- **To try it** — Say **load it**.
```

## "load it"
1. If boss-rush has uncommitted work beyond `.import` / `project.godot` / `default_bus_layout.tres` churn, ask whether to save it first. If he says yes, commit and push it to its current branch. Never discard it.
2. Discard the churn, `git fetch`, check out the PR branch.
3. Run the headless `--quit` parse check.
4. Tell him: click into Godot, reload, press F5.

## "approved" on a Pixel branch
- Follow `playtest-approve.mdc` (merge into main, push, back to main, delete the branch).
- Remove the `ready-to-test` label and comment "Approved by Nathan" on the PR.

## "not yet: <reason>"
- `gh pr comment` with his words.
- Swap the label to `needs-changes`.
- Switch boss-rush back to `main`. Pixel picks it up from there.

## Who does what (advisory)
If Nathan asks Cursor for a Pixel-type job, mention once that it's usually a Pixel job. If he insists, do it.

**Cursor (Nathan directly)**
- Balance numbers
- Card/monster rules and abilities
- Bugs found while playing
- Small UI tweaks
- Adding cards/monsters with placeholder art
- Small tweaks to one existing visual
- Publishing to itch

**Pixel**
- New art and animation (sprites, frames, PixelLab)
- Screen redesigns (mockup first)
- Big visual passes across many files (title intro, wheel monster art)
- Visual consistency audits
- Repo cleanups and recovery

**Gray zone** (ask Nathan once, then go with his answer)
- A UI tweak that needs new art
- A new card or monster that also needs final art: Cursor adds it with placeholder art, Pixel draws it
- Visual bugs that touch many files
